    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0058" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/1041: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzalez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-07T18:00:00-05:00">May 7, 1937—6 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        9:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. The President and the Minister for Foreign Affairs continue inquiry as to the
                    Department’s reaction vis-à-vis the memorandum submitted with my despatch 748,
                    April 17.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d32-f1"/> When may I expect instructions in the
                    premises?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzalez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d32-f1" n="6" xml:id="d32-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; memoranda submitted with this despatch covered conversations
                    reported in telegram No. 22, April 17, 7 p.m., <ref target="#pg46">p.
                    46</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
